WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
- I think July 1st was the
first day of recession.

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:05.572 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think the numbers on GDP's
gotta come out July 28th,

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:07.574
and we'll find out
if it's two quarters

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:11.277
of economy declining, and
then it'll become official,

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:13.346
some economists will say that.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.949 align:start size:97% position:3%
Now, CNN, I don't know if
you saw the article last week

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:20.954 align:start size:97% position:3%
by CNN saying, some experts
are saying we're in recession,

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:24.858
but why is it that it's
eight white economists

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.626 align:start size:84% position:16%
that are saying
we're in recession?

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:27.694
- That's... Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:28.962 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Saw this article.
- Yeah.

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:30.430
- When comes down to recession,

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.866
nobody cares what color you are.

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:35.735 align:start position:0%
And they said, these economists
are not diverse enough,

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:38.171
there's no African
American economist...

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:41.474 align:start size:97% position:3%
In America, the African
American population is 13%,

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:43.510
but only 3% are economists.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:46.012
and this percent is this,
but that percent is this.

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:47.280
And I said, look,

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.985
in America, 24% of the
population is Hispanic.

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:56.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
But in the NBA, it's
only one Hispanic player.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:58.458 align:start size:88% position:13%
What a racist
organization the NBA is,

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:00.060
why don't you guys go a
little bit more diverse

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.294
and hire some Hispanics?

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:03.329
There is no Iranian
basketball player.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:04.764
I'm offended that you
guys don't have any

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:07.067
Iranian basketball
players in the NBA.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.302
So you hear comments like
this people are making

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:11.938 align:start size:88% position:13%
to get people
distracted from the fact

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:15.308
that we're in recession,
it's what's happening.

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.877
(gentle music)

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:24.951 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin and joining
me today is the founder

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:27.087 line:0%
and CEO of Valuetainment,

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:30.423 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
host of the PBD
Podcast and author

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:32.892
of "Your Next Five Moves: Master

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:36.362 align:start size:97% position:3%
the Art of Business
Strategy", Patrick Bet-David.

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.665
Finally, welcome to
the Rubin Report.

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:40.233
- It's great to be on.

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.502
- Good to see you, my friend.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:46.439
We are both relatively
new Floridians, so I feel

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:47.707
we should start there.

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:49.175 align:start size:88% position:13%
Do you have anything you
wanna tell the people

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:50.276
about life in Florida?

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:52.812
- I gotta tell you.

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:55.415 align:start position:0% line:0%
I lived in LA 20 some years
minus the time in the military.

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:59.786 line:0%
I lived five years in Dallas,
Texas, which was fantastic.

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:01.821
I kept one of my
companies there,

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:05.125 align:start position:0%
but then Florida, if
California and Texas could make

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:06.359
a baby, it would be Florida.

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:08.394
Could get the lifestyle,

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.697
and you get the taxes, they
kind of leave you alone.

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:13.800
So we're in love
living in Florida.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.603 align:start size:88% position:13%
- So you moved the
company for what was it?

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:17.937
Five years in Dallas?

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:20.206
And then what caused
you to leave Texas?

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:21.908
Because Texas is pretty good.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:23.443
You ain't paying
the taxes there.

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:25.011 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's a nice
lifestyle over there.

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:29.382
Was it purely weather and
tropical leave related?

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:30.617
- Yeah, that's a good question.

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:33.052
So for me, we were at a
point where we outgrew

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:34.521
the headquarters,

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:36.923
and Valuetainment and the
insurance company were

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:38.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the same headquarters,
same office.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:41.327
And then it was either
I'm gonna sign a lease

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:43.730 align:start position:0%
of a few years with
Valuetainment in Dallas and kind

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.298
of move them to a
different building.

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:48.101
Or if I'm moving, that's
the time to make the move.

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:51.204
So at the time when this
decision was being made,

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:54.240
it was at the beginning
of COVID and my wife

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.742
and I, we were looking

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:57.510 align:start size:97% position:3%
at New York because if we're
running a media company,

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.078
a media company you
gotta be in a place

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:02.549 align:start position:0%
where you can recruit executives
from the media company,

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:04.484
you can recruit talent
to wanna live there...

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:07.754 align:start size:97% position:3%
So we said, Greenwich, New
York, great, it's right there,

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:10.590 align:start position:0%
it's the Mecca, you can
compete, the market's available.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
We looked at Tennessee
because the state's taxes.

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:15.295
And then we looked at
potentially going back

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:18.431
to Newport Beach, California,
because media, again, there,

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:19.933
but COVID happened.

00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:21.501 align:start size:84% position:16%
Everything kind of
moved away from there.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:23.336
We always go to Florida.

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:25.471
And then I knew

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.173 align:start size:97% position:3%
Valuetainment and the media
company would be a lot

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:30.777
easier to recruit people
to south Florida than any

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:31.644
of the other locations.

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.613
So lifestyle was there.

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:34.881
I got four kids now,

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:38.117
10 and 8 and 6, and my
daughter just turned 1.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:40.587
So we got a family. That's
a younger startup family.

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:43.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
We gotta be in a place
that's supports education,

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:45.458
all of that combined together.

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:47.460
Finally we said south
Florida's place to go.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.329
And then obviously
the rest is history.

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:51.798
- And I have seen the
video of the house

00:03:51.798 --> 00:03:54.601
on YouTube and it's not bad.

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:57.470
Let's just say, it's not bad.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:00.773
- Two bedroom condo.
It's a very nice place.

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:02.709
We like it. We're
very happy with it.

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:03.876
- Yeah.

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:05.712 align:start size:88% position:13%
Two bedroom condo might
be under the house

00:04:05.712 --> 00:04:07.680 align:start size:97% position:3%
that you're rocking over
there on the water in Florida.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.249
Absolutely beautiful.

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:12.585 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I know my audience
knows you from the business

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
side of things and mostly
from the podcast side

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:16.289
of things and we'll get
into some of that stuff.

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:18.258 align:start size:97% position:3%
But can you just tell people
who don't know your bio

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:20.693
a little bit about growing
up in Iran and just some

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:24.530
of the who, how you got to
where you are kind of stuff?

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:27.800
- Born and raised in Iran,
lived there for 10 years

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.269
in Tehran, Iran.

00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:32.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
During the revolution
with the Shah, I was born

00:04:32.005 --> 00:04:35.808 align:start size:97% position:3%
October 18th, '78, four
months later, he was in exile,

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:36.643
they kicked him out.

00:04:36.643 --> 00:04:37.910
Then Khomeini showed up.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:40.313 align:start size:88% position:13%
Then the military was
in shambles because 2000

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:42.448 align:start size:84% position:16%
of his leaders were
reporting to the Shah.

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:43.916
Khomeini got rid of 'em.

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:46.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
Saddam saw that as an
opportunity. He attacked.

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:48.454 align:start size:81% position:19%
Half a million
people got killed.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:51.090
Six weeks after Khomeini dies...

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.593 align:start size:88% position:13%
This is around July
15th of '89, we escape,

00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:56.095
I go to Germany with
my mom and my sister.

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:58.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
We lived at a refugee camp
for a year and a half.

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:00.266
And then from Germany,
we came to the States.

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:02.001
I went to Glendale, California.

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:03.603 align:start size:88% position:13%
Right after high school
I joined the army,

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:05.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
went to the 101st Airborne
Division air assault,

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:07.173
and then got out of the army.

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:08.441
I wanted to be a bodybuilder.

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:09.942
I was gonna be the
next Mr. Olympia,

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:11.377
you know, Arnold
Schwartzenegger.

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:14.080 align:start size:97% position:3%
I was gonna win Mr. Olympia,
going to be an actor,

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.716
marry a Kennedy and then
one day run for governor.

00:05:16.716 --> 00:05:18.818 align:start size:97% position:3%
But then I met a girl named
(indistinct) who worked

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:20.253
at Morgan Stanley Dean Witter,

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:23.389 align:start position:0%
she told me about Morgan
Stanley Dean Witter, I was 21...

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:25.725
And she said, this is
how I make a living.

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:26.693
It's a great industry.

00:05:26.693 --> 00:05:28.161
I started working

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:30.897
on Morgan Stanley Dean
Witter a day before 9/11.

00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:32.465
And then I stayed
in the industry.

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:35.268 align:start size:97% position:3%
Seven and a half years
later, I was in Transamerica.

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:36.636
I was a year at the Morgan,

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:38.871 align:start size:84% position:16%
seven and a half
years, Transamerica.

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:40.707
And then October of
'09 started my own

00:05:40.707 --> 00:05:42.141
insurance company, PHP.

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:45.812 align:start size:97% position:3%
We grew that from 66 agents
to 20,000 plus agents,

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:49.949
150 offices nationwide, and
then accidentally started

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:52.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
a YouTube channel that
turned into media company,

00:05:52.185 --> 00:05:54.921 align:start size:97% position:3%
Valuetainment, and then
obviously the rest is history.

00:05:54.921 --> 00:05:57.724 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So I love how you say that
all with just such ease.

00:05:57.724 --> 00:05:59.625
I mean, I know you've
told that story...

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a million stories
within that story.

00:06:01.094 --> 00:06:02.729
I know you've said it
a million times before,

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:05.365 align:start size:88% position:13%
but the reason I wanted
you to say it was

00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:08.234
because you are as much as
anyone I think I've ever had

00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:09.702
on the show, the living,

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:11.371
breathing example of what
the American dream is.

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:12.939
Now, how could that possibly be?

00:06:12.939 --> 00:06:14.607 align:start size:81% position:19%
You are a brown
skinned immigrant.

00:06:14.607 --> 00:06:17.810
I thought that this is
the most racist place,

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.846 align:start size:88% position:13%
I thought we hate people
from the Middle East,

00:06:19.846 --> 00:06:20.680
et cetera, et cetera.

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:22.348
How do you do it?

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:23.683 align:start size:84% position:16%
- You know, with
the power of levity.

00:06:23.683 --> 00:06:25.084
Let me give you an idea
what I mean by the power

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:28.654
of levity, and the
power of not taking

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:31.224
everything personally
and crying about it.

00:06:31.224 --> 00:06:36.229
So I'm in the army, and one
time, one of these soldiers,

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.799 align:start size:97% position:3%
private, I'm in boot camp
with these guys and they said,

00:06:39.799 --> 00:06:40.600
so where are you from?

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:41.868
I said, I'm from Iran.

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:43.403
He says, what do you
mean you're from Iran?

00:06:43.403 --> 00:06:46.506 align:start size:97% position:3%
I said, I'm from Iran. So
how are you in the military?

00:06:46.506 --> 00:06:48.007
Aren't you, are
you a US citizen?

00:06:48.007 --> 00:06:49.509
I said, no, I got a green card.

00:06:49.509 --> 00:06:52.845 align:start size:97% position:3%
How do you get into the
military as a Iranian citizen?

00:06:52.845 --> 00:06:55.548
And you're now in our army?

00:06:55.548 --> 00:06:57.183 align:start size:84% position:16%
I said, can you
guys keep a secret?

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:58.651
They said, yeah, what's up.

00:06:58.651 --> 00:07:00.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, honestly, I'm
kinda like an underground

00:07:00.119 --> 00:07:02.789
spy operation right now,
I'm trying to take all the-

00:07:02.789 --> 00:07:04.223
(Dave laughs)

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:06.092 align:start size:84% position:16%
And by the way, these
guys believed it.

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:08.261
And it was to the point
where my Sergeant had

00:07:08.261 --> 00:07:09.462
to come and talk to me about it.

00:07:09.462 --> 00:07:11.030
And we laughed about it.

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:13.266
But obviously there's
some levity to it.

00:07:13.266 --> 00:07:15.435
I remember gonna Alabama
one time and the waiter

00:07:15.435 --> 00:07:17.904
at Waffle House, we were
on the way to Panama City,

00:07:17.904 --> 00:07:21.240
Florida to party for
like at Club La Vela,

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:23.910
and this Panama City waiter's
just looking at me angled,

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:27.346 align:start size:97% position:3%
and he's like, I've never
seen a nose like that before.

00:07:27.346 --> 00:07:31.017
I said, this is what you
call a legit qualified nose

00:07:31.017 --> 00:07:33.486
from the Middle East, you
guys don't have stuff like

00:07:33.486 --> 00:07:35.688 line:0%
this in America,
we have it in Iran.

00:07:35.688 --> 00:07:38.391 align:start position:0% line:0%
I've never met an Iranian
before. I said, I'm an Iranian.

00:07:38.391 --> 00:07:41.027 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
Anyways. Then I go and I start
working at Morgan Stanley.

00:07:41.027 --> 00:07:43.396 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's a very interesting
story what happens one time,

00:07:43.396 --> 00:07:46.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got into the LDS market,
clients who were LDS.

00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:48.701 align:start size:81% position:19%
And it's a very
good market to get

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:50.303
into when you're managing money,

00:07:50.303 --> 00:07:52.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're gonna get into
different kind of markets,

00:07:52.305 --> 00:07:53.840
car wash owners, doctors...

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:55.908
One of the markets
I got into was LDS.

00:07:55.908 --> 00:07:57.910 align:start size:84% position:16%
And this one business
owner I sat with,

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:00.179
I go into their house,
it's right after 9/11.

00:08:01.614 --> 00:08:03.049
And they said, can you tell
us about your background?

00:08:03.049 --> 00:08:05.084 align:start size:97% position:3%
I said, sure, born and raised
in Iran, all this stuff.

00:08:05.084 --> 00:08:07.019 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I said, now I'm at Morgan
Stanley, managing money

00:08:07.019 --> 00:08:08.221
and helping our families.

00:08:08.221 --> 00:08:09.455
And she says, look,

00:08:09.455 --> 00:08:10.823
we don't mind doing
business with anybody

00:08:10.823 --> 00:08:13.159
from Morgan Stanley, but
we would like you to be

00:08:13.159 --> 00:08:15.828 align:start position:0%
somebody else with a background
that we can relate to.

00:08:15.828 --> 00:08:18.631
Quite frankly, after what
happened with the 9/11,

00:08:18.631 --> 00:08:20.366 align:start size:97% position:3%
we feel a little bit
uncomfortable doing business

00:08:20.366 --> 00:08:22.201
with somebody from
the Middle East.

00:08:22.201 --> 00:08:26.472
Now, in that situation, I can
say, how dare you say that?

00:08:26.472 --> 00:08:28.107 align:start size:81% position:19%
And go cry and
complain about it.

00:08:28.107 --> 00:08:29.942
I said, totally understand.

00:08:29.942 --> 00:08:34.080
Left, brought back my partner,
they met, they did business.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:36.449
We split commission. We
were happy with it, done.

00:08:36.449 --> 00:08:39.986
Moral of the story is, I
don't care who you are.

00:08:39.986 --> 00:08:42.121 align:start size:97% position:3%
If you're a white, black,
Asian, Middle Eastern, tall,

00:08:42.121 --> 00:08:44.790 align:start size:88% position:13%
short, fat, skinny,
educated, not educated,

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.092
you got a beard, you
don't have a beard,

00:08:46.092 --> 00:08:47.894
you have a mustache, you
don't have a mustache...

00:08:47.894 --> 00:08:50.830
Everyone's getting judged.
Whether you like it or not.

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:54.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the reason why this
is a topic I'm bringing up

00:08:54.867 --> 00:08:57.904
is because as much as
everyone's judging us,

00:08:57.904 --> 00:08:59.105
we're also judging people.

00:08:59.105 --> 00:09:00.439
So if you get to judge others,

00:09:00.439 --> 00:09:01.707
why can't they judge you and I?

00:09:01.707 --> 00:09:04.644
So the challenge is
how we react to it.

